<title>EGYPT: YIELD FALLS ON EGYPTIAN 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD FALLS ON EGYPTIAN 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 8.800 percent at Wednesday's auction from 8.825 percent at the previous auction on July 30.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 900 million pounds and accepted bids for 997.800 million. Bills worth 1,003.050 million pounds mature on Aug 14.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 6, 1997 (Oct 30, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.800 percent (8.825)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 997.800 million (991.375 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,199.800 million (1.216.500 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.600 - 8.813 percent (8.499 - 8.872)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.600 - 10.002 percent (8.499 - 10.002)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 36 (57)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 47 (65)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
